From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: <author>
Date: <date>
Subject: [PATCH] ac/surface: force 4KB swizzle for mip-chained render targets on gfx12

On gfx1201 (Navi 48 / RX 9070 XT), rendering into a color surface that
has a mip chain and uses the ADDR3_256B_2D swizzle mode leaves a
deterministic anti-diagonal 16x16-tile corruption at non-power-of-two
pitches. The pattern is byte-identical run to run: for each 16x16-tile
macro block the misplaced tiles sit along the anti-diagonal (x_tile =
~y_tile), matching a pipe-bank interleave mismatch rather than a cache
or coherency issue.

The 256B swizzle is not pipe-interleaved (pipeBankXor / tile_swizzle is
only computed for swizzle modes >= 4KB), so `surf->tile_swizzle` is 0.
But the color pipeline still interleaves writes across the memory banks
as if the surface used a >=4KB swizzle, so writes targeting mip levels
land in the wrong bank and read back as stale or zeroed data.

Both radeonsi and RADV are affected because the swizzle is selected in
shared `gfx12_select_swizzle_mode()`. RADV usually avoids it in practice
by binding restricted per-level views (MAX_MIP=1), but a full-chain view
reproduces the exact same corruption.

The smallest swizzle mode that avoids the corruption is 4KB, so force
4KB_2D for color render-target surfaces that have a mip chain. This only
affects mip-chained color renderable surfaces; single-mip surfaces and
sampler-only (NO_RENDER_TARGET) surfaces keep their previous layout.

Fixes rendering corruption into texture mip levels (glGenerateMipmap /
glBlitFramebuffer / FBO rendering) seen as black 32x32 blocks in GTK4 /
loupe on gfx1201.

---

 src/amd/common/ac_surface.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c b/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c
index c5d3a82323b..8409d5345ca 100644
--- a/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c
@@ -3699,6 +3699,21 @@ static unsigned gfx12_select_swizzle_mode(struct ac_addrlib *addrlib,
         (!get_out.validModes.sw2d256B && !get_out.validModes.swLinear)))
       return ADDR3_4KB_2D;
 
+   /* A color surface with a mip chain must not use the 256B swizzle:
+    * rendering into such a surface on Navi 48 (gfx1201) produces a
+    * deterministic anti-diagonal tile corruption at non-power-of-2 pitches
+    * (the 256B swizzle is not pipe-interleaved, but the color pipeline still
+    * interleaves writes across banks assuming a >=4KB swizzle). This also
+    * covers upload-only mip-chained textures (TRANSFER_DST | SAMPLED without
+    * COLOR_ATTACHMENT usage): blit-based mipmap generation renders into them
+    * anyway. Only depth/stencil surfaces are excluded. Force 64KB.
+    * (4KB also corrupts at 3840x2160 with >=8 mip levels and DCC; 64KB is
+    * the layout AMD's PAL/Windows driver selects and is clean at all tested
+    * sizes.) */
+   if (!(flags & RADEON_SURF_Z_OR_SBUFFER) && in->numMipLevels > 1 &&
+       get_out.validModes.sw2d64kB)
+      return ADDR3_64KB_2D;
+
    assert(get_out.validModes.sw2d256B || get_out.validModes.swLinear);
 
    if (get_out.validModes.sw2d256B && get_out.validModes.swLinear)
